<!--
    Type-recovery campaign, coreutils `fmt` -O2 (stripped): `main` @0x26a0 calls
    one static function three times and kuna renders three different arities,
    the longest reading a local nothing assigns.

        unsigned long v9;  // rdx        <- never assigned
        unsigned long v11; // rdx        <- never assigned
          v10 = v9;  ...  v10 = v11;
          v12 = sub_3700(stdin,"-",v10);   // three arguments
          v3  = sub_3700(stdin,v6);        // two
          v12 &= sub_3700(v5);             // one

    DWARF says `fmt(FILE *f, char const *name)`: two parameters.

    Root cause (P4, active-input trial scoring).  `Heritage::guardCalls`
    (heritage.cc:1444) plants an INDIRECT *creation* for a killed-by-call
    register that is also a possible OUTPUT location of the callee's model.
    rdx is one on x86-64, because a 16-byte value returns in rax:rdx, and
    `AncestorRealistic::enterNode` (funcdata_varnode.cc:2043) answers
    pop_success for exactly that op, recording `ParamTrial::setIndCreateFormed`.
    With `onlyOpUse` satisfied the trial is active and
    `ParamListStandard::fillinMap` marks every active trial used, so a register
    the caller never wrote for this call becomes its trailing argument.
    Upstream reads that same bit back on the RETURN side only
    (`ParamListStandardOut::fillinMap`, fspec.cc:1721), which is why stock
    Ghidra emits the identical three-argument call and names the phantom
    `extraout_RDX`.

    The fixture is the same construct, hand assembled.  rdx at the call is a
    two-input join and NEITHER input is a value the caller put there for this
    call: on one path `clobber` destroyed the register (and its own first act is
    a call, so `calleepreserves` cannot narrow the killed set), on the other an
    `idivl` left its remainder in edx while the caller went on to use only the
    quotient.  That second half is the `% 200` term of the fmt witness, and it
    is the only non-clobber shape the rule accepts: upstream scores a trial
    formed by a remainder exactly like one formed by an indirect creation, on
    the return side (`ParamListStandardOut::fillinMap`, fspec.cc:1721).
    `target`'s first act is a call, so `calleedeadarg` cannot prove rdx dead
    there either.

    Stage / sub-stage: P4 "active-input-trial-scoring".  The P0 assertion
    `option argclobber on|off` decides whether the trailing argument of a call
    may be dropped when nothing on the caller's side put a value in its
    register.

    Pass 1 (`option argclobber off`, the shipped default) reproduces the BUG:
    `target` takes a third argument built out of the clobber and the dead
    remainder.
    Pass 2 (`option argclobber on`) is the FIX: the trailing argument is gone,
    the dead remainder goes with it, and the quotient the caller really uses is
    untouched.
-->
